learnings:
  - 'The whole renaissance (Tasks spearhead + two-way GitHub sync + governance + UI) shipped as v7.3.0 via the same loop that worked all session: audit/design → build per-round → verify state DIRECTLY (build + tests + LIVE smoke against the real system) → ship-per-round (lore+changelog+commit+push) → PR → dogfood. Live integration testing against the real GitHub repo caught 2 bugs (gh arg format owner/repo#N vs bare number; ESM require() in readSyncConfig) that 468 green unit tests missed — for any external-system integration, a live round-trip before claiming done is non-optional.'
  - The Tasks board lives in the GITIGNORED local task store (.paradigm/tasks/), while the GitHub issues are the SHARED durable record — so the two-way sync's `task done → issue closes` IS the right cleanup/dogfood mechanism, not a workaround. When asked to 'close tasks', closing them propagates to GitHub automatically.
  - A malformed .purpose (e.g. unquoted colon-space in a long description) is SILENTLY SKIPPED by the indexer, so its whole directory's symbols vanish from the index — fixing the Tasks .purpose YAML restored the spearhead's coverage. Use block scalars (>-) for long descriptions. This recurred this session (it's the open T-...-011 index-integrity papercut), reinforcing that the purpose-writer should auto-quote.
